#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:1
msgid "Binary Installation on Ubuntu"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:3
msgid ""
"Rotary binaries are published for Ubuntu Noble (24.04) and Ubuntu Resolute "
"(26.04) via the nightly packages repository at `packages.osrfoundation.org`. "
"To install all of them, the metapackage `gz-rotary` can be installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:9
msgid ""
"Rotary is a rolling, unstable stream. Packages are updated nightly and "
"breakage is expected. For production use, install a named release such as "
"[Jetty](https://gazebosim.org/docs/jetty) instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:14
msgid "First install some necessary tools:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:16
msgid ""
"sudo apt-get update\n"
"sudo apt-get install curl lsb-release gnupg\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:21
msgid "Then install Gazebo Rotary:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:23
msgid ""
"sudo curl https://packages.osrfoundation.org/gazebo.gpg --output /usr/share/"
"keyrings/pkgs-osrf-archive-keyring.gpg\n"
"echo \"deb [arch=$(dpkg --print-architecture) signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/"
"pkgs-osrf-archive-keyring.gpg] http://packages.osrfoundation.org/gazebo/"
"ubuntu-stable $(lsb_release -cs) main\" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/"
"gazebo-stable.list > /dev/null\n"
"echo \"deb [arch=$(dpkg --print-architecture) signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/"
"pkgs-osrf-archive-keyring.gpg] http://packages.osrfoundation.org/gazebo/"
"ubuntu-nightly $(lsb_release -cs) main\" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/"
"gazebo-nightly.list > /dev/null\n"
"sudo apt-get update\n"
"sudo apt-get install gz-rotary\n"
msgstr ""
"sudo curl https://packages.osrfoundation.org/gazebo.gpg --output /usr/share/"
"keyrings/pkgs-osrf-archive-keyring.gpg\n"
"echo \"deb [arch=$(dpkg --print-architecture) signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/"
"pkgs-osrf-archive-keyring.gpg] http://packages.osrfoundation.org/gazebo/"
"ubuntu-stable $(lsb_release -cs) main\" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/"
"gazebo-stable.list > /dev/null\n"
"echo \"deb [arch=$(dpkg --print-architecture) signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/"
"pkgs-osrf-archive-keyring.gpg] http://packages.osrfoundation.org/gazebo/"
"ubuntu-nightly $(lsb_release -cs) main\" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/"
"gazebo-nightly.list > /dev/null\n"
"sudo apt-get update\n"
"sudo apt-get install gz-rotary\n"

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:31
msgid ""
"All libraries should be ready to use and the `gz sim` app ready to be "
"executed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:33
msgid ""
"Head back to the [Getting started](getstarted) page to start using Gazebo!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:37
msgid "Server-only installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:39
msgid ""
"For headless and CI environments where the GUI is not needed, the `gz-sim-"
"server` package provides a lightweight alternative. It installs only the "
"Gazebo simulation server (`gz-sim-server`) without any GUI or Qt "
"dependencies, resulting in a significantly smaller installation footprint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:44
msgid ""
"After configuring the repository (same as above), install the server-only "
"package:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:47
msgid "sudo apt-get install gz-sim-server\n"
msgstr "sudo apt-get install gz-sim-server\n"

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:51
msgid ""
"The server-only package includes the DART physics engine and the core "
"simulation server plugins. To start a headless simulation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:54
msgid "/usr/libexec/gz/sim/gz-sim-server <world_file.sdf>\n"
msgstr "/usr/libexec/gz/sim/gz-sim-server <world_file.sdf>\n"

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:59
msgid ""
"The server-only binary is installed at `/usr/libexec/gz/sim/gz-sim-server`, "
"which is not in the `PATH` by default. The regular `gz sim -s` command is "
"not available in the server-only installation since it requires the full `gz-"
"sim-cli` package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:66
msgid "Uninstalling binary install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:68
msgid ""
"If you need to uninstall Gazebo Rotary or switch to a source-based install, "
"run the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:71
msgid "sudo apt remove gz-rotary && sudo apt autoremove\n"
msgstr ""

